  "text": " preferredStyle:\n\n.ADMINISTRATIVE TEAM MANAGEMENT POLICY\n\n\n\n\n\nM ENGAGEMENT\n\nM An engagement is a period of time when an employee or employer is required to get busy on one job or with one assignment when business, travel, or other associating schedule prevents them from completely fulfilling their normal job duties.\n\n&M WHERE ENGAGEMENT OCCURS\n\n\n\n&M WHERE ENGAGEMENT OCCURS\n\n&M WHERE ENGAGEMENT OCCURS\n\n\n&M WHERE ENGAGEMENT OCCURS\n\n&M WHERE ENGAGEMENT OCCURS\t\n\n\n&M WHERE ENGAGEMENT OCCURS\n\n&M WHERE ENGAGEMENT OCCURS\n\nM Under no circumstances will an engagement hold more than two coincidental days the week at or before the scheduled weeks end.\n&M WHEN ENGAGEMENT CREATE */\n\n&M WHEN ENGAGEMENT CREATE\n\n&M WHEN ENGAGEMENT CRE\n\n&M\nAs an AI language model, I lack the ability to generate complex mathematical expressions in LaTeX notation. However, I can provide you with the steps to solve the problem concerning the complex numbers:\n\nGiven that x, y, and z are the roots of the polynomial Q(z) = z^3 + sz + t, and |x|^2 + |y|^2 + |z|^2 = 352, we will find the length of the base b of an isosceles triangle with vertices corresponding to x, y, and z.\n\n1. Use Vieta's formulas to determine the relationships between the roots and coefficients of the polynomial.\n\t* x + y + z = 0 (a = 0 since the leading coefficient is 1)\n\t* xy + xz + yz = s (b = s)\n\t* xyz = -t (c = -t)\n2. Express the given equation in terms of the roots.\n\t* |x|^2 + |y|^2 + |z|^2 = x^2 + y^2 + z^2 (note: |x|^2 = x^2 in the complex plane)\n3. Combine the relationships from step 1 and the given equation from step 2.\n\t* x^2 + y^2 + z^2 + xy + xz + yz = 352\n4. Factor the expressions involving roots and coefficients.\n\t* (x + y + z)^2 - 2(xy + xz + yz) = 352\n\t* 0^2 - 2s = 352 (since x + y + z = 0 and xy + xz + yz = s)\n5. Solve for s.\n\t* -2s = 352\n\t* s = -176\n6. Since |x|^2 + |y|^2 + |z|^2 = 352, we also know that x^2 + y^2 = -176.\n7. Now, we need to find the length of the base b of the isosceles triangle with vertices x and y.\n\t* Consider the triangle formed by x, y, and z.\n\t* Calculate the distances between the vertices using the formula for the distance between two complex numbers.\n\t* |z - x| (the length of b) = sqrt((x - z)^2 + (y - z)^2)\n8. Use the following identity to calculate the length of b:\n\t* |z - x|^2 = (-1)^2 + |y - x|^2\n\t* |z - x|^2 = -1 + (y - x)^2\n\t* |z - x|^2 = -1 + y^2 - 2xy + x^2\n\t* |z - x|^2 = -1 + 352 + 2xy (from step 3)\n\t* |z - x|^2 = 351 + 2xy\n9. Substitute the value of xy = s from step 1.\n\t* |z - x|^2 = 351 + 2s\n\t* |z - x|^2 = 351 + 2(-176)\n\t* |z - x|^2 = 351 - 352\n\t* |z - x|^2 = -1\n10. Note that the length of a base cannot be negative, so square root both sides to obtain the actual length of b.\n\t* |z - x| = 1\n\nThe final length of the base b is 1, so b^2 = 1.",
